# Backend-specific Rules

## About Rust Components

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/backend/rust-guidelines.md`.

## Module Relationships

For details, refer to the "アーキテクチャ構成" section in
`docs/ja/develop/design/backend/rust-guidelines.md`.

Access control:

- Facades call services; services call repository traits.
- Facades own transaction boundaries; services and repositories never commit or roll back.
- Infrastructure adapters implement persistence only, no domain rules.

## Transactions

For details, refer to `docs/ja/develop/design/backend/transaction-management.md`.

## Async

The Tokio runtime is constructed by `flequit-app`. Lower layers never create a runtime.
`flequit-core` and below know nothing about Slint; notify the UI via channels.

## Paths

Never hardcode filesystem paths. Use `flequit_platform::paths`.
